WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.868
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:06.950
PRIYANKA VERGADIA:
Give me a minute,

00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:08.780
and I'll show you how
Compute Engine can

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:11.840
help you move existing
workloads to Google Cloud.

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:14.650
Compute Engine delivers
scannable and high performance

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:17.802
virtual machines running
in Google's data centers.

00:00:17.802 --> 00:00:19.760
You can select the right
machine for your needs

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:22.370
from predefined or
custom machine types.

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:24.510
It's easy-- just select
the type of machine

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:26.080
and where you want it.

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:29.420
Choose general purpose machines
for apps, databases, and web

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:31.910
servers, or memory
optimized machines

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:36.380
for in-memory databases, SAP
HANA, and real-time analytics.

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:39.260
Or compute optimized machines
for high performance computing,

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:42.680
financial modeling,
gaming, and RGPUs

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:45.560
to accelerate computationally
intensive workloads

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:48.410
like machine learning
or medical analysis.

00:00:48.410 --> 00:00:51.800
Using Compute Engine, you can
live migrate between hosts

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:53.180
without rebooting.

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:56.310
This keeps your apps running,
even during maintenance.

00:00:56.310 --> 00:00:58.350
It provides right
size recommendations

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:02.030
so you can resize your machine
type depending on your usage.

00:01:02.030 --> 00:01:04.700
You pay for what you use, and
you can increase those savings

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:07.820
by applying committed use
and sustained use discounts.

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:10.160
For further savings,
check out Preemptible VMs.

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:13.970
These are low-cost, short-term
instances suited for batch jobs

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:15.950
and fault tolerant workloads.

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:18.860
Use Compute Engine to
migrate your existing systems

00:01:18.860 --> 00:01:21.230
into Google Cloud,
run databases,

00:01:21.230 --> 00:01:24.980
do financial modeling, or
even run Windows workloads.

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:27.270
Next time you're
thinking about migrating

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:29.580
your apps to the cloud
quickly, take a minute

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:31.260
to look at Compute Engine.

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:35.330
For more info, check out
cloud.google.com/compute.

